# Foxglove Layout Format Rules

## Required Top-Level Structure
All Foxglove layouts must have these exact fields:
```json
{
  "configById": {},
  "globalVariables": {},
  "userNodes": {},
  "linkedGlobalVariables": [],
  "playbackConfig": { "speed": 1 },
  "layout": {}
}
```

## Panel Type Format
- **Correct**: Use panel IDs as strings in layout: `"first": "Plot!gps"`
- **Incorrect**: Never use `"type": "panel"` in layout structure
- **Panel IDs**: Must match entries in `configById` section

## Valid Panel Types
- `Plot!name` - Data plotting panels
- `Map!name` - Map visualization panels  
- `3D!name` - 3D visualization panels
- `Gauge!name` - Gauge/indicator panels
- `Image!name` - Image display panels
- `Table!name` - Data table panels
- `Text!name` - Text display panels
- `StateTransitions!name` - State machine panels
- `RosOut!name` - ROS log panels

## Layout Structure
- Use panel ID strings directly: `"first": "Plot!gps"`
- For nested layouts, use `"direction"` and `"first"/"second"` properties
- Never nest panel objects with `type` and `config` in layout

## Configuration Reference
- All panel configurations go in `configById` section
- Panel IDs in `configById` must match panel IDs used in `layout`
- Use existing working layouts as templates: [argo_ros2.json](mdc:foxglove/argo_ros2.json)

## Common Errors to Avoid
- Missing `linkedGlobalVariables: []` field
- Using `"type": "panel"` instead of proper panel IDs
- Mismatched panel IDs between `configById` and `layout`
- Invalid panel type names (must end with `!` and descriptive name)